  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Four Points Technology L L C obligated $737M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Four Points Technology L L C won 735 awards in the current fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $1M. Four Points Technology L L C obligations are down 12.7% year over year. Four Points Technology L L C has moved through a few peaks and troughs since FY21: obligations were $641M in FY21, $618M in FY22, $769M in FY23, $911M in FY24, and $845M in FY25. Four Points Technology L L C concentrates work in one dominant NAICS market. Four Points Technology L L C received $727M under Other Computer Related Services in FY2026 to date, with smaller amounts in medical and manufacturing categories such as Surgical and Medical Instrument Manufacturing at $9.1M and Computing Infrastructure Providers, Data Processing, Web Hosting, and Related Services at $1.9M. Four Points Technology L L C also sells to a broad set of agencies, with the largest buyers listed across health, security, and civilian portfolios.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the largest buyers of Four Points Technology L L C?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer at $233M. The Department of Homeland Security follows at $148M, then the Social Security Administration at $89M, and the Department of Health and Human Services at $63.6M. The Department of Commerce, NASA, SEC, GSA, Department of Transportation, and Department of Justice round out the top ten buyers."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and product lines does Four Points Technology L L C serve?",
        "body": "Other Computer Related Services is the dominant market at $727M. Four Points Technology L L C also has work in Surgical and Medical Instrument Manufacturing at $9.1M and Computing Infrastructure Providers, Data Processing, Web Hosting, and Related Services at $1.9M, with smaller amounts in software, HVAC manufacturing, and pharmaceutical-related NAICS codes."
      }
    ]
  },
